IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division G (General): sections 87 to 90.2.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. What each rule means for a person is in the seat layer, cp5-seat.l4.
--
-- Section 87 lets the Minister use census returns to find a person's age; section 88 presumes a person who has disappeared to be
-- dead; section 89 (regulation-making power) is machinery and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table); sections 90 and 90.1 make
-- certain conduct an offence or the ground of an administrative penalty; section 90.2 gives the Minister powers of inspection and of
-- requiring documents, with the protections of the occupant and of a third party.
-- Regulation 51 (the Regulations, piece cr2) fixes the conditions that section 87 leaves to the regulations; it is read in the rule for
-- section 87, and cr2 encodes the regulation itself.
-- Where the text speaks of the Minister's opinion or satisfaction, the opinion or satisfaction is a plain input (a conditional answer).

-- out of range: section 66 (piece cp4): the duty to return a payment or an excess amount, a plain fact in s 90(1)(c)
-- out of range: section 105 (piece cp6): the agreements under which information from Statistics Canada may be disclosed, a plain fact in regulation 51(b) as read in s 87
-- out of range: regulation 51 (piece cr2): read in s 87

§ `Part II, Division G -- General (sections 87 to 90.2)`

§§ `Section 87 -- census information`

-- Regulation 51(a): the request to Statistics Canada must be in the form prescribed by the Chief Statistician, bear the signed consent
-- of the person (or of the person or agency who applied for them) and give the information needed for a proper search of the census
-- records; regulation 51(b): the information obtained must not be disclosed except to officers, clerks or employees of the Department
-- of Employment and Social Development or as an agreement under section 105 requires.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:492 | 51 For the purposes of section 87 of the Act, the following are prescribed as the conditions subject to which any information specified in that section respecting the age of any applicant or beneficiary or the applicant’s or beneficiary’s spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner is obtainable from Statistics Canada on request and for the purpose specified in that section:
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:493 | (a) the request to Statistics Canada must
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:494 | (i) be made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician,
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:495 | (ii) bear the signed consent of the applicant, beneficiary, spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner or of the person or agency that made the application on their behalf or, where there is no such person or agency, any other person or agency who would have been entitled to make the application on their behalf, and
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:496 | (iii) provide such information as may be necessary to enable a proper search to be made of the census records for the purpose of obtaining the information requested; and
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:497 | (b) information obtained under section 87 of the Act must not be disclosed to any person other than an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development or other than as required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act.
@ref Reg 51 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:492-497)
GIVEN `the request is made in the form prescribed by the Chief Statistician` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request bears the signed consent of the person or of the person or agency who applied on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives the information needed for a proper search of the census records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information obtained will not be disclosed except to an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development or as an agreement under section 105 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 87 — the conditions prescribed by regulation 51 are met` `the request is made in the form prescribed by the Chief Statistician` `the request bears the signed consent of the person or of the person or agency who applied on their behalf` `the request gives the information needed for a proper search of the census records` `the information obtained will not be disclosed except to an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development or as an agreement under section 105 requires` MEANS
        `the request is made in the form prescribed by the Chief Statistician`
    AND `the request bears the signed consent of the person or of the person or agency who applied on their behalf`
    AND `the request gives the information needed for a proper search of the census records`
    AND `the information obtained will not be disclosed except to an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development or as an agreement under section 105 requires`

-- src:2511 | Census information
-- src:2512 | 87 Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, for the purpose of ascertaining the age of any applicant or beneficiary, or of an applicant’s or a beneficiary’s spouse or common-law partner or former spouse or former common-law partner, the Minister is entitled to obtain from Statistics Canada, on request, any information respecting that person’s age that is contained in the returns of any census taken more than thirty years before the date of the request.
@ref Act s 87 (src:2512)
GIVEN `the purpose is to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary, or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `day the census was taken` IS A DATE
      `day of the request` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 87 — the Minister is entitled to obtain from Statistics Canada the information about the person's age that the census returns contain` `the purpose is to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary, or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner` `day the census was taken` `day of the request` `the prescribed conditions are met` MEANS
        `the purpose is to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary, or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner`
    AND `the prescribed conditions are met`
    -- the returns of any census taken more than thirty years before the date of the request
    AND `day the census was taken` BELOW `the date a time limit before a date goes back to` `day of the request` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 30)

§§ `Section 88 -- presumption as to death`

-- src:2513 | Presumption as to death
-- src:2514 | 88 (1) Where a contributor or beneficiary, or a contributor’s or beneficiary’s spouse or common-law partner or former spouse or former common-law partner, has, either before or after the coming into force of this section, disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the person is dead, the Minister may determine the date for the purposes of this Act on which that person’s death is presumed to have occurred, and thereupon that person shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act to have died on that date.
@ref Act s 88(1) (src:2514)
GIVEN `the person is a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the person is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Minister determines as the date on which the person's death is presumed to have occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 88(1) — the date on which the person is deemed to have died` `the person is a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner of one` `the person has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the person is dead` `the date the Minister determines as the date on which the person's death is presumed to have occurred` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner of one`
       AND `the person has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the person is dead`
    THEN `the date the Minister determines as the date on which the person's death is presumed to have occurred`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2515 | Change of date
-- src:2516 | (2) If, after having determined the date of a person’s death pursuant to subsection (1), the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different from that determined, the Minister may determine a different date of death, in which case the person shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act to have died on that different date and the Minister shall forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable if the determination of death had not been made.
@ref Act s 88(2) (src:2516)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the different date the Minister determines` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 88(2) — the date on which the person is deemed to have died after the Minister determines a different date` `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different` `the different date the Minister determines` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` AND `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different`
    THEN `the different date the Minister determines`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (2) ends: "the Minister shall forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable if the determination
-- of death had not been made". Subsection (3) says the same where the person appears.
@ref Act s 88(2) (src:2516)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a different date of death under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88(2) — the Minister must forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable if the determination of death had not been made` `the Minister has determined a different date of death under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the Minister has determined a different date of death under subsection (2)`

-- src:2517 | Where person appears
-- src:2518 | (3) If, after having determined the date of a person’s death pursuant to subsection (1), the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the person is alive, the Minister shall forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable in respect of the person had that determination not been made.
@ref Act s 88(3) (src:2518)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88(3) — the Minister must forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable in respect of the person had the determination not been made` `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the person is alive` MEANS
    `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection (1)` AND `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the person is alive`

-- src:2519 | Benefits cease
-- src:2520 | (4) Where any benefit has been paid to any person as a result of the determination of another person’s death pursuant to this section and the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that that other person is alive, the benefit shall forthwith cease to be payable and any such benefit paid prior to the Minister’s being satisfied that the person is alive shall be deemed to have been validly paid.
@ref Act s 88(4) (src:2520)
GIVEN `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88(4) — the benefit ceases forthwith to be payable` `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive` MEANS
    `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` AND `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive`

@ref Act s 88(4) (src:2520)
GIVEN `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88(4) — the benefit paid before the Minister was satisfied that the other person is alive is deemed to have been validly paid` `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive` MEANS
    `a benefit has been paid to a person as a result of the determination of another person's death under this section` AND `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive`

-- src:2521 | Death certificates issued by other authorities
-- src:2522 | (5) For the purposes of this section, the Minister is not bound by the issuance or revocation of a death certificate by any other authority.
@ref Act s 88(5) (src:2522)
GIVEN `another authority has issued or revoked a death certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88(5) — the Minister is bound by the issuance or revocation of a death certificate by another authority` `another authority has issued or revoked a death certificate` MEANS
    -- "the Minister is not bound": whatever the other authority did
    FALSE

§§ `Section 90 -- offences`

-- src:2552 | Offence and punishment
-- src:2553 | 90 (1) Every person who
-- src:2554 | (a) knowingly makes a false or misleading statement in any application or declaration or makes any application or declaration that by reason of any non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading, or obtains any benefit payment by false pretences,
-- src:2555 | (b) being the payee thereof, negotiates or attempts to negotiate any cheque for a benefit to which he is not entitled, or
-- src:2556 | (c) knowingly fails to return any cheque or the amount of any benefit payment or any excess amount as required by section 66,
-- src:2557 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Act s 90(1) (src:2553-2557)
GIVEN `the person knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made an application or declaration that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained a benefit payment by false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, being the payee, negotiated or attempted to negotiate a cheque for a benefit to which the person is not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly failed to return a cheque, the amount of a benefit payment or an excess amount as section 66 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90(1) — the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the person knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration` `the person made an application or declaration that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading` `the person obtained a benefit payment by false pretences` `the person, being the payee, negotiated or attempted to negotiate a cheque for a benefit to which the person is not entitled` `the person knowingly failed to return a cheque, the amount of a benefit payment or an excess amount as section 66 requires` MEANS
    -- (a) knowingly makes a false or misleading statement, or makes an application or declaration false or misleading by non-disclosure
    --     ("knowingly" is read as governing the first limb only: NOTES.md, fork F16), or obtains a benefit payment by false pretences
        `the person knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration`
     OR `the person made an application or declaration that by reason of non-disclosure of facts is false or misleading`
     OR `the person obtained a benefit payment by false pretences`
    -- (b) being the payee, negotiates or attempts to negotiate a cheque for a benefit to which the person is not entitled
     OR `the person, being the payee, negotiated or attempted to negotiate a cheque for a benefit to which the person is not entitled`
    -- (c) knowingly fails to return a cheque, a benefit payment or an excess amount as required by section 66
     OR `the person knowingly failed to return a cheque, the amount of a benefit payment or an excess amount as section 66 requires`

-- src:2558 | Limitation period
-- src:2559 | (2) Any proceedings under this Act in respect of an offence may be commenced at any time within, but not later than, five years after the Minister becomes aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings.
@ref Act s 90(2) (src:2559)
GIVEN `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 90(2) — the last day on which proceedings in respect of an offence may be commenced` `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 5)

@ref Act s 90(2) (src:2559)
GIVEN `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` IS A DATE
      `day the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90(2) — proceedings in respect of the offence may be commenced on that day` `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` `day the proceedings are commenced` MEANS
    `day the proceedings are commenced` AT MOST `s 90(2) — the last day on which proceedings in respect of an offence may be commenced` `day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings`

-- src:2560 | Saving
-- src:2561 | (3) No proceeding shall be commenced under this section or the Criminal Code for an act or omission if a penalty for that act or omission has been imposed under section 90.1.
@ref Act s 90(3) (src:2561)
GIVEN `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90(3) — no proceeding shall be commenced under section 90 or the Criminal Code for the act or omission` `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 90.1` MEANS
    `a penalty for the act or omission has been imposed under section 90.1`

§§ `Section 90.1 -- administrative monetary penalties`

-- src:2564 | Penalty for misrepresentation, etc.
-- src:2565 | 90.1 (1) The Minister may impose on a person a penalty for each of the following acts or omissions if the Minister becomes aware of facts that in the Minister’s opinion establish that the person has
-- src:2566 | (a) made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:2567 | (b) made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:2568 | (c) knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person’s earnings for a period for which the person received disability benefits;
-- src:2569 | (d) received or obtained by cheque or otherwise a benefit payment to which the person knew that they were not entitled, or a benefit payment that the person knew was in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which they were entitled, and did not return the cheque or the amount of the benefit payment, or the excess amount, as the case may be, without delay; or
-- src:2570 | (e) participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in any of paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref Act s 90.1(1) (src:2565-2570)
GIVEN `the Minister has become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person's earnings for a period for which the person received disability benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person knew they were not entitled, or in excess of the amount to which they were entitled, and did not return it without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participated in, assented to or acquiesced in one of those acts or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.1(1) — the Minister may impose a penalty on the person` `the Minister has become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the acts or omissions` `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading` `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` `the person knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person's earnings for a period for which the person received disability benefits` `the person received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person knew they were not entitled, or in excess of the amount to which they were entitled, and did not return it without delay` `the person participated in, assented to or acquiesced in one of those acts or omissions` MEANS
        `the Minister has become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish that the person has done one of the acts or omissions`
    AND (   `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `the person made a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that the person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts`
         OR `the person knowingly failed to declare to the Minister all or some of the person's earnings for a period for which the person received disability benefits`
         OR `the person received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person knew they were not entitled, or in excess of the amount to which they were entitled, and did not return it without delay`
         OR `the person participated in, assented to or acquiesced in one of those acts or omissions`)

-- src:2571 | Purpose of penalty
-- src:2572 | (1.1) The purpose of the penalty is to promote compliance with this Act and not to punish.
@ref Act s 90.1(1.1) (src:2572)
DECLARE `cp5 Purpose of a penalty under section 90.1` IS ONE OF
    `to promote compliance with this Act and not to punish`

@ref Act s 90.1(1.1) (src:2572)
`s 90.1(1.1) — the purpose of the penalty` MEANS `to promote compliance with this Act and not to punish`

-- src:2573 | Maximum penalty
-- src:2574 | (2) The Minister may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than $10,000.
@ref Act s 90.1(2) (src:2574)
`s 90.1(2) — the most the Minister may set as the penalty for each act or omission` MEANS 10000

@ref Act s 90.1(2) (src:2574)
GIVEN `the number of acts or omissions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 90.1(2) — the most the Minister may set as the penalty for the acts or omissions` `the number of acts or omissions` MEANS
    `the number of acts or omissions` TIMES `s 90.1(2) — the most the Minister may set as the penalty for each act or omission`

@ref Act s 90.1(2) (src:2574)
GIVEN `the amount set as the penalty for the act or omission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.1(2) — the amount set for the act or omission is within the maximum` `the amount set as the penalty for the act or omission` MEANS
    `the amount set as the penalty for the act or omission` AT MOST `s 90.1(2) — the most the Minister may set as the penalty for each act or omission`

-- src:2575 | Limitation on imposition of penalties
-- src:2576 | (3) A penalty shall not be imposed on a person under subsection (1) if
-- src:2577 | (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person; or
-- src:2578 | (b) five years have passed since the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission.
@ref Act s 90.1(3) (src:2576-2578)
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `day the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.1(3) — a penalty shall not be imposed on the person` `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person` `day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` `day the penalty would be imposed` MEANS
    -- (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person
        `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the person`
    -- (b) five years have passed since the day on which the Minister became aware of the act or omission
    --     (the fifth anniversary of that day counts as five years passed: NOTES.md, fork F17)
     OR `day the penalty would be imposed` AT LEAST `the date a time limit ends` `day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 5)

-- src:2579 | Rescission, etc., of penalty
-- src:2580 | (4) The Minister may rescind the imposition of a penalty under subsection (1), or reduce the penalty,
-- src:2581 | (a) on the presentation of new facts;
-- src:2582 | (b) on being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact;
-- src:2583 | (c) on being satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future; or
-- src:2584 | (d) on being satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor.
@ref Act s 90.1(4) (src:2580-2584)
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.1(4) — the Minister may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` `new facts have been presented` `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor` MEANS
        `new facts have been presented`
     OR `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact`
     OR `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future`
     OR `the Minister is satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor`

§§ `Section 90.2 -- administration and enforcement`

§§§ `Subsection 90.2(1) -- the definitions`

-- src:2587 | Interpretation
-- src:2588 | 90.2 (1) The definitions in this subsection apply in this section.
-- src:2589 | document includes moneys, securities, books, records, letters, accounts, statements (financial or otherwise), correspondence, memoranda, film, microform, videotape, photographs, machine-readable records and other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics, and any copy or printout of any of them. (document)
@ref Act s 90.2(1) "document" (src:2589)
DECLARE `cp5 Kind of thing that a document includes` IS ONE OF
    `moneys as a kind of document`
    `securities as a kind of document`
    `books as a kind of document`
    `records as a kind of document`
    `letters as a kind of document`
    `accounts as a kind of document`
    `statements, financial or otherwise as a kind of document`
    `correspondence as a kind of document`
    `memoranda as a kind of document`
    `film as a kind of document`
    `microform as a kind of document`
    `videotape as a kind of document`
    `photographs as a kind of document`
    `machine-readable records as a kind of document`
    `other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics as a kind of document`
    `a copy or printout of any of those things as a kind of document`
    `another kind of thing that the definition of document does not list`

@ref Act s 90.2(1) "document" (src:2589)
GIVEN thing IS A `cp5 Kind of thing that a document includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(1) — a thing is a document` thing MEANS
    -- "document includes ...": the list is not closed, so a thing outside it is not decided (NOTES.md, fork F4 of the keel, followed here)
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `another kind of thing that the definition of document does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2590 | dwelling-house means the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence and includes
-- src:2591 | (a) a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway; and
-- src:2592 | (b) a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence. (maison d’habitation)
@ref Act s 90.2(1) "dwelling-house" (src:2590-2592)
GIVEN `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and is being used as such a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(1) — a place is a dwelling-house` `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` `the place is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and is being used as such a residence` MEANS
        `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence`
     OR `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway`
     OR `the place is a unit designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and is being used as such a residence`

-- src:2593 | judge means a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises or a judge of the Federal Court. (juge)
@ref Act s 90.2(1) "judge" (src:2593)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(1) — a person is a judge` `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` MEANS
    `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` OR `the person is a judge of the Federal Court`

§§§ `Subsections 90.2(2) to (5) -- inspections, and entry to a dwelling-house`

-- src:2594 | Inspections
-- src:2595 | (2) The Minister may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, examine any document that relates or may relate to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit and, for that purpose, the Minister may
-- src:2596 | (a) subject to subsection (3), enter any premises or place where the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept; and
-- src:2597 | (b) require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to give the Minister all reasonable assistance and to answer all proper questions relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act and, for that purpose, require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to attend at those premises or that place with the Minister.
-- src:2598 | Warrant required to enter dwelling-house
-- src:2599 | (3) Where the premises or place referred to in subsection (2) is a dwelling-house, the Minister may not enter that dwelling-house without the consent of the occupant except under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (4).
@ref Act s 90.2(3) (src:2599)
GIVEN `the place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(3) — the Minister may enter the dwelling-house` `the place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry` MEANS
    (NOT `the place is a dwelling-house`) OR `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` OR `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry`

@ref Act s 90.2(2) (src:2595-2597)
GIVEN `it is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(2)(a) — the Minister may enter the premises or place` `it is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place` `the place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry` MEANS
        `it is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place`
    -- subject to subsection (3)
    AND `s 90.2(3) — the Minister may enter the dwelling-house` `the place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the Minister's entering` `a warrant has been issued under subsection (4) authorizing the entry`

-- Paragraph (b) is not made subject to subsection (3): the duty to assist and attend does not depend on entry (NOTES.md, fork F27).
@ref Act s 90.2(2) (src:2595-2597)
GIVEN `it is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(2)(b) — the person must give the Minister all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend at the place` `it is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place` `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the place` MEANS
        `it is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the Minister believes that a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit is or should be kept at the place`
    AND `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the place`

-- src:2600 | Warrant
-- src:2601 | (4) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter a dwelling-house subject to the conditions that may be specified in the warrant, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:2602 | (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2);
-- src:2603 | (b) entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act; and
-- src:2604 | (c) entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused.
@ref Act s 90.2(4) (src:2601-2604)
GIVEN `the Minister has applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(4) — a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter the dwelling-house` `the Minister has applied ex parte` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2)` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused` MEANS
        `the Minister has applied ex parte`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2)`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused`

-- src:2605 | Other access to document
-- src:2606 | (5) Where the judge is not satisfied that entry into that dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act but is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused, the judge may
-- src:2607 | (a) order the occupant of the dwelling-house to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document; and
-- src:2608 | (b) make any other order that is appropriate in the circumstances to carry out the purposes of this Act.
@ref Act s 90.2(5) (src:2606-2608)
GIVEN `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(5) — a judge may order the occupant to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document and make any other appropriate order` `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused` MEANS
    `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused`

§§§ `Subsections 90.2(6) to (11) -- requirements to provide documents or information`

-- src:2611 | Unnamed persons
-- src:2612 | (7) The Minister shall not impose on a person, in this section referred to as a “third party”, a requirement under subsection (6) to provide information or a document relating to one or more unnamed persons unless the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection (8).
@ref Act s 90.2(7) (src:2612)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(7) — the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (8)` MEANS
    (NOT `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons`) OR `the Minister has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (8)`

-- src:2609 | Requirement to provide documents or information
-- src:2610 | (6) Despite any other provision of this Act, the Minister may, subject to subsection (7), for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require that any person provide, within the reasonable time that is stipulated in the notice, any information or additional information or any document.
@ref Act s 90.2(6) (src:2610)
GIVEN `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(6) — the person must provide the information or document within the time stipulated in the notice` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice stipulates a reasonable time` `the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party under subsection (7)` MEANS
        `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the notice was served personally or by confirmed delivery service`
    AND `the notice stipulates a reasonable time`
    AND `the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party under subsection (7)`

-- src:2613 | Judicial authorization
-- src:2614 | (8) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may, subject to the conditions that the judge considers appropriate, authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement under subsection (6) relating to one or more unnamed persons, in this section referred to as the “group”, where the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:2615 | (a) the person or group is ascertainable; and
-- src:2616 | (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act.
@ref Act s 90.2(8) (src:2614-2616)
GIVEN `the Minister has applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(8) — a judge may authorize the Minister to impose the requirement on the third party` `the Minister has applied ex parte` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` MEANS
        `the Minister has applied ex parte`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act`

-- src:2617 | Service of authorization
-- src:2618 | (9) Where an authorization is granted under subsection (8), the authorization shall be served together with the notice referred to in subsection (6).
@ref Act s 90.2(9) (src:2618)
GIVEN `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(9) — the authorization has been served as the subsection requires` `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)` `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection (6)` MEANS
    (NOT `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)`) OR `the authorization was served together with the notice referred to in subsection (6)`

-- src:2619 | Review of authorization
-- src:2620 | (10) Where an authorization is granted under subsection (8), a third party on whom a notice is served under subsection (6) may, not later than 15 days after the service of the notice, apply to the judge who granted the authorization or, if that judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court for a review of the authorization.
@ref Act s 90.2(10) (src:2620)
GIVEN `day the notice was served on the third party` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 90.2(10) — the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `day the notice was served on the third party` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `day the notice was served on the third party` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 15)

@ref Act s 90.2(10) (src:2620)
GIVEN `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `day the notice was served on the third party` IS A DATE
      `day the third party applies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(10) — the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)` `day the notice was served on the third party` `day the third party applies` MEANS
        `an authorization has been granted under subsection (8)`
    AND `day the third party applies` AT MOST `s 90.2(10) — the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `day the notice was served on the third party`

-- src:2621 | Powers on review
-- src:2622 | (11) On hearing an application under subsection (10), a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (8)(a) to (d) have been met, and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if the judge is satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Act s 90.2(11) (src:2622)
-- The text says "paragraphs (8)(a) to (d)"; subsection (8) has only paragraphs (a) and (b) (NOTES.md, fork F26 and finding 9).
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(11) — the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted` `the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` MEANS
    NOT (`the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` AND `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act`)

@ref Act s 90.2(11) (src:2622)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(11) — the judge may confirm or vary the authorization` `the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` MEANS
    `the judge is satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable` AND `the judge is satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act`

§§§ `Subsections 90.2(12) and (13) -- copies as evidence, and compliance`

-- src:2623 | Copies as evidence
-- src:2624 | (12) Where a document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with this section, the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided may make, or cause to be made, one or more certified copies of it and any such copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Act s 90.2(12) (src:2624)
GIVEN `the document was inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 90.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy was made, or caused to be made, by the person who inspected or examined it or to whom it was provided, and certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(12) — the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force` `the document was inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 90.2` `the copy was made, or caused to be made, by the person who inspected or examined it or to whom it was provided, and certified` MEANS
    `the document was inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 90.2` AND `the copy was made, or caused to be made, by the person who inspected or examined it or to whom it was provided, and certified`

-- src:2625 | Compliance
-- src:2626 | (13) No person shall interfere with any person doing anything that the person is authorized under this section to do or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing.
@ref Act s 90.2(13) (src:2626)
GIVEN `the person interfered with another person, or prevented or attempted to prevent another person, from doing something` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person was authorized under section 90.2 to do it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90.2(13) — the person contravened the prohibition on interfering with or preventing a person doing what section 90.2 authorizes` `the person interfered with another person, or prevented or attempted to prevent another person, from doing something` `the other person was authorized under section 90.2 to do it` MEANS
    `the person interfered with another person, or prevented or attempted to prevent another person, from doing something` AND `the other person was authorized under section 90.2 to do it`
